# Project Guidelines

## Project Requirements Document (PRD)

- Always consult the PRD file [prd.md](mdc:prd.md) at the root of the project
- When implementing features, ensure they align with the specifications in the PRD
- If you need to make changes to the codebase that would affect requirements, update the PRD accordingly
- The PRD is the source of truth for project requirements and should be kept up to date

## Task Management

- Keep the [tasks.md](mdc:tasks.md) file at the root of the project up to date with project progress
- Mark completed tasks with `- [x]` checkmarks in markdown
- Leave pending tasks as `- [ ]` 
- Add new tasks when features expand
- Organize tasks under appropriate version sections
- Create subtasks for complex features
- Update task status after implementing features